SUMMARY:Moonlight Hike - Bob Hunter Park - Moderate
DESCRIPTION:GTA Hiking & Stuff\n**_I may have to change the location of th
 e hike if the Park Warden won't keep the gates open for us._**\n\nWe will 
 hike at a moderate pace for 6 - 7 km in 2 hrs or less. Please bring a head
 lamp or a flashlight. Let's hope it will be clear so we can see the sun at
  night. The moon can get bright enough to turn off our headlamps while we 
 hike\, so if you haven't experienced a night hike\, come out and enjoy the
  adventure. Just don't be the last in line.😬\n\nThe trail weaves throug
 h the forest\, along a pathway\, and in open medows\, giving us many oppor
 tunities to admire the moon. This hike is about the energy of the moon. Th
 e trails are icy\, so bring your Crampons.\n6\n_After the hike\, we can ag
 ree on a pub/restaurant and go for something to eat and/or a drink._\n\n**
 Note**\n\n* Arrive on time! Please cancel if you can't make it.\n* Know yo
 ur limits! Hike within it.\n* Dress for the conditions.\n* Be aware and pr
 epared for ticks.\n* Free Parking.\n* No Dogs.\n* The hike will be cancele
 d if the weather doesn't cooperate.\n\n***Hike leaves promptly at 8:00 PM*
 **\n\n**LEGAL DISCLAIMER AND LIABILITY INFORMATION:**\n\nBy RSVP'ing and p
 aying the event fee (if applicable)\, you are confirming that you have rea
 d\, understand and accept the following:\n\n1. GTA Hiking Meetup is a priv
 ate group. Attending events is voluntary by you as a member. Participation
  in any activity with us is at your own risk.\n2. By joining this event as
  a member you agree to indemnify and hold harmless its organizers\, co-org
 anizers\, assistant organizers\, event hosts\, and other members from all 
 claims or liability of every type (including court costs and legal fees) f
 or injury or death to any person or for damage to property\, loss of perso
 nal property or any other wrongful act arising out of or relating to your 
 participation as a member. This agreement applies to you and to other pers
 ons (as your guests) who may accompany you in these endeavors.\n3. You als
 o agree to hold the organizers as well as other group members harmless. By
  participating voluntarily in the group\, you expressly waive any and all 
